# memchentic Tool Routing

Gate: if memchentic is not connected/ready, skip all memchentic tools.

Prefer the smallest tool that answers the question. Default coding turns stay
on recall + capture tools only.

## Everyday (default rules already cover)

| Job | Tool |
| --- | --- |
| Reusable guides before approach | `guide_find` |
| Hybrid search → digests | `find` |
| Full body | `open` |
| Path-scoped digests | `about_path` |
| Save durable entry | `remember` |
| Save / strengthen guide | `guide_write` |
| Patch entry | `revise` |

## Situational

| Job | Tool |
| --- | --- |
| Who am I / spaces | `me`, `space_list`, `space_show` |
| Create a team | `space_create` (user principal; not admin API key) |
| Paginated list | `browse` |
| Time window | `since` |
| Tag filter | `by_tag` |
| Move entry | `relocate` |
| Delete | `forget` |
| Provenance | `trace` |
| Near-dups / expiry hygiene | `overlap_report` |

## Entry types (closed v1)

`fact` · `preference` · `decision` · `instruction` · `feedback` · `insight` ·
`note`

## Explicitly not in v1

Multi-agent queues/leases/meshes, vision search, server-side “reflect the
whole graph,” third-party note-app bridges, and ops diagnose/heal packs.
Grow the **memchentic** surface later when there is a real need — do not
invent foreign tool names.
